    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "788bd7d5_eddcbbff",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 6035
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-07T21:53:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s for readability and IPC-ability. I\u0027m going to `std::vectory`-fiy the fixed-size arrays, so that we don\u0027t IPC the extra entries that we don\u0027t use.\n\nIf I leave this as structure-of-arrays, then I\u0027ll have to have 3 arrays that all need to be the same size (for x, y, and m), which is more error-prone than 1 array of (x,y,m) values.\n\nI\u0027d gone with structure-of-arrays because it matches the [metadata set specification](https://doc.smpte-doc.org/st2094-50-private/main/#sec-metadata-set) and because I have a suspicion it may be marginally faster to evaluate.",
      "parentUuid": "4f89a5bf_0543bb9e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 16,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 16,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "ad6a5129c5b786a336418844a511e7702f9c9c2e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
